00:27:59.640 --> 00:28:00.473
We'll get to those.

00:28:00.473 --> 00:28:01.680
We'll be plenty of time for the Q&amp;A.

00:28:01.680 --> 00:28:03.750
We have such a good showing here today

00:28:03.750 --> 00:28:05.000
which we appreciate and also see

00:28:05.000 --> 00:28:06.690
a lot of people in the know

00:28:06.690 --> 00:28:07.820
who work on the side of doing it,

00:28:07.820 --> 00:28:08.754
who have made important contributions

00:28:08.754 --> 00:28:11.160
to sort of the way scholarship, et cetera.

00:28:11.160 --> 00:28:14.040
So we look forward to
your questions as well.

00:28:14.040 --> 00:28:15.140
I guess I can just get, start out off

00:28:15.140 --> 00:28:16.590
kind of in a general sense,

00:28:16.590 --> 00:28:17.860
David, if you could just kind of tell us

00:28:17.860 --> 00:28:19.640
a little bit, you know,

00:28:19.640 --> 00:28:23.470
what possesses somebody to
translate, how to do it?

00:28:23.470 --> 00:28:26.600
You were talking about
sort of this obsession

00:28:26.600 --> 00:28:29.360
or this obsession,
obsessive method that he had

00:28:29.360 --> 00:28:30.400
with sort of revisiting, you know

00:28:30.400 --> 00:28:31.560
the sonnet and these different things.

00:28:31.560 --> 00:28:33.840
While I would imagine that
that kind of obsession

00:28:33.840 --> 00:28:35.320
probably also falls on the shoulder

00:28:35.320 --> 00:28:37.680
of a translator of Sarduy as well.

00:28:37.680 --> 00:28:38.930
So if you could maybe just tell us kind of

00:28:38.930 --> 00:28:42.770
what gets you started down this path.

00:28:42.770 --> 00:28:43.770
- Thank you, Shawn.

00:28:43.770 --> 00:28:48.110
I fell in love with Sarduy's,
poems from the beginning.

00:28:48.110 --> 00:28:52.080
I, you know, from the first
moment I encountered them.

00:28:52.080 --> 00:28:55.320
I found a small edition of poems,

00:28:55.320 --> 00:28:58.490
also published in the
eighties called (indistinct)

00:28:58.490 --> 00:29:00.560
I was a master's program in Spanish

00:29:00.560 --> 00:29:02.200
at the University of Virginia.

00:29:02.200 --> 00:29:05.100
And they give you contributed also

00:29:05.100 --> 00:29:09.750
to the 1985 publication that
I just was reading from.

00:29:09.750 --> 00:29:12.567
And these brilliantly complex on it.

00:29:12.567 --> 00:29:15.889
And I thought, Oh, these
I know the sonnet form.

00:29:15.889 --> 00:29:18.310
I love that anyway.

00:29:18.310 --> 00:29:21.460
And I thought it would be
a super accessible (laughs)

00:29:21.460 --> 00:29:25.119
when this was my first
encounter with this poem.

00:29:25.119 --> 00:29:27.413
And I found very quickly that

00:29:27.413 --> 00:29:30.040
that was absolutely not the case,

00:29:30.040 --> 00:29:35.040
but something about his
ability to infuse language

00:29:36.520 --> 00:29:39.050
with so many things happening at once

00:29:39.970 --> 00:29:41.677
was really compelling with me,

